# NOT READ BY THE KAGGLE CLI. This file is a manifest, not a config.
#
# `kaggle datasets version -p .` uploads the working tree verbatim; nothing consults this
# list. Treating it as enforcement cost a training session: runs/ and data/shards/ were
# uploaded, and notebook 03 then resumed a 25-epoch CPU smoke checkpoint and mixed
# _smoke_fall.npz into the real fall corpus.
#
# Use instead:  python scripts/publish_code_dataset.py -m "why this version exists"
# which stages only src/ scripts/ configs/ weights/ into a temp dir, verifies the repo
# contract against the STAGED copy, and refuses to upload if any artefact slipped in.
#
# Excluded from the behaviorsense-code Kaggle dataset upload.
#
# MSMT17 is the reason this file exists: 2.7 GB of licence-restricted person crops that
# NO notebook reads. Tau is already fitted and committed (results/reid_eval.md), so
# uploading it would multiply the dataset size by 36x, buy nothing, and put a
# redistribution-restricted corpus on cloud storage. Excluding it takes the upload from
# 2.7 GB to 74 MB.

MSMT17/
Market-1501*/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.git/
runs/
data/shards/
data/*.db
results/embeddings/
.venv/
